      "body": "## Motivation\n\nWith `tool_choice=\"required\"` or a named function, the GLM grammar is `assistant_turn ::= thinking_block text_block tool_call_blocks` with an unbounded `text_block`. EOS stays masked until `<tool_call>` appears, so a model that keeps writing ordinary text runs to `max_tokens` with no tool call. Seen with GLM-5.3-Flash under conflicting instructions; the reproduction is in #42458. There is no separate GitHub issue for this grammar bug (#13514 was the earlier JSON-grammar variant, fixed in v0.5.6.post2).\n\nPredecessor #42458 removes `text_block` for required selection. Review there noted that GLM models usually emit a short text preamble before the call, so this PR keeps the preamble and bounds it instead.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `generate_glm_grammar`: when `required and functions`, `text_block ::= ( <sep> [^<]{0,256} )?`, so the call must start within 256 characters. Excluding `<` also keeps every GLM special token out of the preamble.\n- `tool_choice=\"auto\"` and requests without tools keep the unbounded `text_block`.\n- `test_required_selection_bounds_text_preamble`: 256 characters of text before the call are accepted for auto, required and named selection; 257 are accepted only for auto; thinking on and off.\n\nKnown limitation: a literal `<` in the preamble (e.g. `a < b`) is rejected under required selection. It is still allowed inside tool-call argument values.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nGrammar construction only; no model forward or kernel changes. `test/registered/unit/function_call/test_function_call_parser.py -k \"Glm47FullAssistantGrammar or Glm4MoeDetector or Glm47MoeDetector\"` passes locally, and the new test fails against the current `main` grammar. No end-to-end argument-quality A/B was run.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40934947407](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40934947407)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40934947307](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40934947307)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40934947402](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40934947402)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n",
